            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>We know this market in detail.</strong> We know that each of the 12 borough offices reviews building applications according to its own practice — anyone who ignores that fails in the revision cycle. We know that Berlin’s sandy soil class 3 to DIN 18196 and an inner-city water table 2 to 4 m below ground demand a pile or raft foundation to DIN 4017/4020. We know that the Adlershof research campus requires vibration isolation for photonics and laser technology, and that a hospital campus in Mitte requires sterile logistics under KhBauVO Berlin. These details are not in our quotation — they are the engineering foundation of every container that leaves our Albstadt works.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Made in Albstadt, turnkey in Berlin.</strong> Final assembly and interior fit-out are carried out with Wesemann furniture at our own works — a factory visit can be planned from either side. North on the A81, east on the A6 and north on the A9 via Würzburg and Nuremberg, the heavy-goods distance is around 720 kilometres; via the Berlin Ring (A10) and the Berlin-Süd, Berlin-Schönefeld or Berlin-Spandau junctions, all Berlin research and hospital sites are directly reachable.
            </p>
            <p>
